{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1405726-on-contagion-and-the-perception-there-of-by-hunters","id":1405726,"title":"On Contagion and the Perception There-of by Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-31T19:58:39-07:00","id":1405726,"title":"On Contagion and the Perception There-of by Hunters","content":"BTB, the effects of Contagion cannot be perceived by mortals without a supernatural template. That being the case, how do Hunters fit into the system? I can't imagine any Hunter doing serious actions on a monster's say so. One could argue that having an Endowment is a reasonable excuse, but then where does that leave Tier 1 and 2 characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T21:13:25-07:00","id":1405740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1405726-on-contagion-and-the-perception-there-of-by-hunters#post1405726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTB, the effects of Contagion cannot be perceived by mortals without a supernatural template.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is to do with that bit in the introduction, I think you're overreading it.<br /> <br /> &quot;It affects every creature capable of perceiving and interacting with the supernatural&quot; by definition includes hunters; just because some aspects of the supernatural are inaccessible to hunters doesn't mean they don't interact with it, else the vast majority of monsters would be completely blind to the Contagion as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:59:53-07:00","id":1406155,"title":"","content":"Hunters would definetly be considered as &quot;interacting&quot; with the supernatural. Being an hunter is practically the act of the human soul clashing against the darkness and knowingly taking a stand against it (at least, in 2e, which was taken into account while writing the Contagion Chronicles). Rejecting the supernatural is a form of interaction with it- as the lack of interaction means being blind to it, closing your eyes as much as possible and pretending you have seen nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:09:22-07:00","id":1406163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1405726-on-contagion-and-the-perception-there-of-by-hunters?p=1406155#post1406155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters would definetly be considered as &amp;quot;interacting&amp;quot; with the supernatural. Being an hunter is practically the act of the human soul clashing against the darkness and knowingly taking a stand against it (at least, in 2e, which was taken into account while writing the Contagion Chronicles). Rejecting the supernatural is a form of interaction with it- as the lack of interaction means being blind to it, closing your eyes as much as possible and pretending you have seen nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that hunters should be counted as \u201cinteracting with\u201d the supernatural for purposes of the Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T18:16:12-07:00","id":1406198,"title":"","content":"As others have said, the act of simply accepting the supernatural exists once seen is enough to interact with it. Hell the Vigil is pseudo mystical to be honest (if not full on so)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T03:19:12-07:00","id":1406246,"title":"","content":"It laso goes about evidence. People ( normal people ) do not see the disease or pandemic on naked eyes - but they still know it's there. People got sick around them, some got hurt, they can get ill themselves and got symptoms. Hunters may not see supernatural phenomena on naked eye - but surely they can see consequences of those on the world. Contagions are maybe supernatural, but are still disease( -ish )...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}